elcontextprotocol/sdk package over stdio. Add a package.json, install @mode=
lcontextprotocol/sdk and zod with npm, and make sure node_modules is in .gi=
tignore.
2. It reads four environment variables: TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID, TWILIO_AUTH_TOK=
EN, TWILIO_BASE_URL and TWILIO_FROM. It calls Twilio's REST API at &lt;TWIL=
IO_BASE_URL&gt;/2010-04-01/Accounts/&lt;TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID&gt;/Messages.jso=
n with HTTP Basic auth (account sid and auth token), sending form fields To=
, From and Body.
3. Give it four tools, each with a clear description:
- send-sms: send one message (to, body). Return the message sid, status and=
 number of segments.
