po. <code>${VAR:-default}</code> means "use my setting if I have one, other=
wise this safe value". If Claude keeps picking Grep over an MCP tool, the t=
ool's description is too thin, which is why the build prompt asks for clear=
 descriptions.</p></div></div>
  <p><strong>If something goes wrong:</strong></p>
  <ul class=3D"plainlist">
    <li><strong>fetch failed or connection refused:</strong> the practice s=
erver isn't running, or a setting says localhost. Start the server again, a=
nd use 127.0.0.1.</li>
    <li><strong>sms shows "failed" in /mcp:</strong> run <code>npm install<=
/code> in the studio folder. If it still fails, ask Claude to put the full =
path to <code>mcp/sms-server.mjs</code> in <code>.mcp.json</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Error 21606:</strong> the From number isn't the practice se=
rver's own. Leave <code>TWILIO_FROM</code> unset so it uses <code>+15551234=
567</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Pending approval:</strong> start <code>claude</code> and ap=
prove the <code>sms</code> server.</li>
  </ul>
</section>
<section class=3D"step" id=3D"step-10" data-step=3D"10">
