ce "./"
- skills/personalize/SKILL.md, copied from our skill, with anything Chirpne=
t-specific made general
- hooks/hooks.json, registering our send guard as a PreToolUse hook on mcp_=
_sms__.*, using ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT} instead of $CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR, plus =
hooks/send-guard.mjs
- agents/sms-reviewer.md: a subagent that reviews message files against the=
 project's brand voice and SMS rules, using only Read, Glob and Grep
- review/findings.schema.json and scripts/review.mjs
- README.md: what's inside and how to install it
Brand voice, subscribers, campaigns, .mcp.json and the mcp/ folder stay in =
each client's own repo. The README should say why.
Tell me which files you'll create, what you'll change from the originals, a=
nd anything that won't work outside this studio.</pre></div>
  <p><strong>Then:</strong> Read the plan. Find one thing it says won't tra=
vel to a new client. Then accept the plan.</p>
  <div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-head"><span class=3D"chip build">B=
UILD</span><span class=3D"code-desc">2 of 3 =C2=B7 After you read the plan<=
/span></div><pre>The plan looks good. Build it. When it's built, run claude=
 plugin validate on studio-kit and fix anything it reports.</pre></div>
  <div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-head"><span class=3D"chip build">B=
UILD</span><span class=3D"code-desc">3 of 3 =C2=B7 Same session</span></div=
><pre>Set up a second, made-up client so I can test studio-kit somewhere ne=
w. Create a folder next to this one called client-two, for a small tea-and-=
snacks cafe chain called Chai Junction, with:
- brand/voice.md: a short voice guide (warm and friendly, no health claims,=
 sender tag "ChaiJunction:", end every message with "Reply STOP to opt out")
- CLAUDE.md: one paragraph about the studio, plus the line @brand/voice.md
- subscribers/subscribers.csv: 6 made-up people in two groups, office-regul=
ars and weekend-families, all with practice numbers from +12025550151 to +1=
2025550156, with the same columns as our subscribers file
- subscribers/CLAUDE.md: our subscriber folder rules, plus a "Groups" secti=
on with one line describing each group
- .claude/rules/sms.md, .mcp.json, package.json and mcp/sms-server.mjs, cop=
ied from this studio, but change the SMS rule's sender tag and link to Chai=
 Junction's (use https://chaijunction.example/winter)
- campaigns/winter-chai/messages/01-hello.md: one short message that follow=
s the SMS rules
Then run npm install and git init in client-two and commit everything there=
. Don't install studio-kit; I'll load it myself.</pre></div>
  <p><strong>Then:</strong> <code>/exit</code>, then <code>cd ..\client-two=
</code>. Start Claude Code with your kit loaded: <code>claude --plugin-dir =
..\studio-kit</code>. Approve the sms server when asked. Keep the practice =
server running.</p>
  <div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-head"><span class=3D"chip check">C=
HECK</span><span class=3D"code-desc">Inside client-two, then paste</span></=
div><pre>Test the studio-kit plugin in this client. Only the personalize sk=
ill may write files.
